["detached, kept, or removed outright" maps to: renderer's `unmount` deactivating `COMPONENT_SHOULD_KEEP_ALIVE` branches, KeepAlive's `onBeforeUnmount` teardown, and `pruneCacheEntry` — in both the runtime-core (DOM) and runtime-vapor implementations.]

```json
[
  {
    "path": "packages/runtime-core/src/components/KeepAlive.ts",
    "from_line": 239,
    "to_line": 253,
    "why": "When the KeepAlive itself is unmounted, this onBeforeUnmount teardown walks every cached branch and decides each one's fate: the branch matching the current subtree keeps its shape flag reset and gets only its deactivated hook invoked (it is unmounted along with KeepAlive), while every other cached branch is removed outright via unmount(cached)."
  },
  {
    "path": "packages/runtime-core/src/renderer.ts",
    "from_line": 2413,
    "to_line": 2424,
    "why": "In the renderer's unmount(), this is the decision point for a keep-alive'd branch vnode being unmounted: if its shapeFlag has COMPONENT_SHOULD_KEEP_ALIVE it is detached/kept by calling ctx.deactivate() (moving it into the storage container) and returning, instead of being torn down."
  },
  {
    "path": "packages/runtime-core/src/components/KeepAlive.ts",
    "from_line": 189,
    "to_line": 201,
    "why": "pruneCacheEntry() decides per cached entry whether it is removed outright (unmount(cached)) or kept (resetShapeFlag(current) because it is the active branch that cannot be unmounted yet), then deletes it from cache/keys."
  },
  {
    "path": "packages/runtime-vapor/src/components/KeepAlive.ts",
    "from_line": 336,
    "to_line": 372,
    "why": "The runtime-vapor counterpart of the KeepAlive unmount teardown: it deactivates the branch matching the current cache key (kept, with deactivated hook queued) and removes every other cached branch outright from the storage container, stopping their kept-alive scopes."
  },
  {
    "path": "packages/runtime-vapor/src/components/KeepAlive.ts",
    "from_line": 287,
    "to_line": 304,
    "why": "The runtime-vapor pruneCacheEntry(): the equivalent decision for a pruned cache entry, removing the branch from the DOM outright unless it is the current branch (which only gets its shape flag unset so it stays to be unmounted normally), then deleting the key and stopping its scope."
  }
]
